{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00377","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00377@rel:R25-11#42576588","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00377","release":"R25-11","content":"function OpenFileWriteOnly [SWS_PER_00377] Upstream: RS_PER_00001 , RS_PER_00004 , RS_PER_00010 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00144 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; UniqueHandle &lt; WriteAccessor &gt; &gt; OpenFileWriteOnly ( ara::core::StringView fileName) noexcept; Opens a file of this File Storage for writing. The file is truncated (corresponding to kTruncate). If the file does not exist, it is created. The file will be closed when the returned UniqueHandle goes out of scope. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/file_storage.h\" class mono Scope class ara::per::FileStorage class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe PerErrc ::kIllegalWrite rollback_semantics class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td fileName td File name of the file. May correspond to the PersistencyFile.file Name of a configured file. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; UniqueHandle &lt; WriteAccessor &gt; &gt; td A Result containing a UniqueHandle for the file. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td Access td Returned if the File Storage is configured as read-only, or if it is configured as write-only-once and the key already exists. td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td no_rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kIntegrityCorrupted td rollback_semantics Returned if stored data cannot be read because the structural integrity is corrupted. td PerErrc ::kValidationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the validity of stored data cannot be ensured. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the decryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kResourceBusy td rollback_semantics Returned if the file is already open, or if DeleteFile, RecoverFile, or ResetFile with the same file name is currently being executed. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for a new file. td PerErrc ::kTooManyFiles td rollback_semantics Returned if the number of files would get larger than the configured maxNumberOfFiles when the file is created. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if checking the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00","text_key":"1f9ee3d69a86"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00377","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"function","name":"OpenFileWriteOnly","module":"PER","cluster":"","page":"classes/cl_ara_per_FileStorage_29266b.html","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R25-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"AP"},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-9c4c62a62e074c38","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Persistency","p":21,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"OpenFileWriteOnly overload on FileStorage","n":7,"cap":"Figure 5.1: Interfaces Provided by Persistency to Other Functional Clusters","sha":"9c4c62a62e074c38d26caaecacd79c748cdb4c3d6c59d9722cf16e20cf33ffce","nser":5,"src":"figure"},{"id":"FIG-fc8ffa29099851b0","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":88,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"OpenFileWriteOnly convenience method","n":1